{"title":"Alexis Ohanian says he’s a ‘techno optimist,’ despite social media’s impact on society (TechCrunch, 2023-10-31T17:21:47+00:00)","text":"Alexis Ohanian says he’s a ‘techno optimist,’ despite social media’s impact on society (TechCrunch, 2023-10-31T17:21:47+00:00)
Does Reddit co-founder Alexis Ohanian have regrets over his creation? The entrepreneur and founder of venture fund Seven Seven Six, speaking at an event at the University of Virginia, espoused a fairly negative view of the current social media landscape and the creator economy — an environment where he says, everyone has “been so trained and conditioned now to just get the likes and retweets, get the upvotes…I wish I could be more optimistic about it, but we’re seeing it play out before our eyes.” Still, he ultimately described himself as a “techno-optimist” — an apparent nod to a16z General Partner Marc Andreessen’s recent diatribe where he claimed technology could solve all our problems.

“Guilty as charged,” Ohanian said, during his interview with Kara Swisher. “I do think that pendulum will swing back. I think even swifter than we realize.”","entities":["TechCrunch","creator economy","technology","Alexis Ohanian says he’s a ‘techno optimist,’ despite social media’s impact on society","Seven Seven Six","Marc Andreessen","a16z","Kara Swisher","University of Virginia","event at the University of Virginia","interview with Kara Swisher","Alexis Ohanian","Reddit","social media"],"facts":["SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? -PUBLISHED_BY-> TechCrunch","Sam Altman backs teens’ startup, Google unveils the Pixel 8 and TikTok tests an ad-free tier -PUBLISHED_BY-> TechCrunch","More from the US v Google trial: vertical search, pre-installs and the case of Firefox/Yahoo -PUBLISHED_BY-> TechCrunch","After warning, the EU opens investigation into X over alleged disinformation -PUBLISHED_BY-> TechCrunch","SBF Trial: The latest updates from the FTX collapse’s courtroom drama -PUBLISHED_BY-> TechCrunch"]}

